  "reason": "Evidence: The best config so far is config_020 (pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted, acc=0.6352). PCA (pca_n2000) outperforms scgpt (0.5176) by a wide margin, avgpool beats transformer (0.5856 vs 0.6352), and weighted fusion slightly edges concat. The one major untested RNA encoder with the best other settings is scvi_n200. Question: Can a learned variational autoencoder (scvi_n200) capture richer RNA structure than a fixed PCA projection while keeping all other components at their empirically best values (imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted)? Why this is the best use: It isolates the single highest-impact untested variable (RNA encoder type) while holding all other knobs at their known-optimal settings, maximizing the chance of either finding a new best or confirming PCA's sufficiency—critical information with only 4 experiments remaining."
}

